This program makes use of a GAN training system teaching a generator to create a map and then use latent space to transform it into a dnd style map. It makes use of a conditional discriminator and a conditional generator to reach this outcome. It uses a dataset of dnd_maps and map_references to train on comparing them one to one while training. When each one trains they are optimized towards a reduction in loss causing constant back and fourth between the generator and the discriminator. For training clarity it makes use of an L1 loss. It was trained on a total of 60 epochs with a result of a good amount of clarity on the resulting map and when the latent space is used a dnd grid can be seen as attempted to be implemented towards the map fitting a change from a normal to a dnd map.
